<title>UK: TOTAL DUTCH HYDROCRACKER TO SHUT SECOND HALF AUG.</title>
<headline>TOTAL DUTCH HYDROCRACKER TO SHUT SECOND HALF AUG.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Total SA said on Wednesday it would shut its 39,000 barrels per day (bpd) hydrocracking unit at its Vlissingen, Netherlands refinery for around one-and-a-half weeks later this month.</p>
<p>The shutdown for a change of catalyst is to take place some time in the second half of August, a senior refinery official said.</p>
<p>No other units at the refinery, which has a crude distillation capacity of 150,000 bpd, will be affected, he added.</p>
<p>--Keyvan Hedvat, London newsroom +44 171 542 8185</p>
</text>
